{
 "encounter_id": "00715",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hello, doctor! I've come for my heart scan results, the echo. I've been worried sick, to be honest, and I told my sister I'd ring her straight after."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let's put your mind at rest as much as we can. First, remind me what's been happening? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Palpitations, mostly. My heart flutters, like a bird in my chest, a few times a week."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And anything else along with it?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Breathless, when I climb the stairs at work. Third floor, no lift. And a bit dizzy sometimes, when it happens."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any chest pain?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No pain. Thank God."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any fainting?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Never fainted, no."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Okay. Your echocardiogram showed that your heart muscle is pumping normally. But one of the valves, the mitral valve, bulges back a little when it closes. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Bulges? Is that bad? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's called mitral valve prolapse, and it's common, especially in young women. Usually harmless. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Usually? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "In most people it never causes trouble. The palpitations you describe can go with it. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. Phew. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me examine you, to make sure it matches the scan. Pulse and pressure first. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Of course. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 84, blood pressure 112 over 70, temperature 36.7, oxygen 99 percent, respiratory rate 14.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that normal? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Completely normal. Breathe for me, I'm listening to your heart. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is it making a noise?",
   "pause": 18.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "There's a click in mid-beat, which is the valve, and no murmur. Your lungs are clear, and there's no swelling of your ankles."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "So it all fits? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It does. I'd say what you're feeling is most likely due to the mitral valve prolapse."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What do I do about it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Mostly nothing. Cut down on caffeine, and keep hydrated. But I'd like to be sure the palpitations are benign, so I'd like to arrange a 48-hour heart rhythm monitor."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "The little box I wear? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Exactly. You wear it, press a button when you feel a flutter, and send it back. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Easy. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in four weeks, when the monitor results are back."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Four weeks. Good. Can I tell my sister it's not serious? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Tell her it's common, usually harmless, and being looked after. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Brilliant. Thank you so much. ~"
  }
 ],
